{"name":"Champagne Grape","hex":"#c5b067","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"champagne","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sparkling white wine made from a blend of grapes, especially Chardonnay and pinot, produced in Champagne, France, by the méthode champenoise.","Any sparkling wine made by the méthode champenoise."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a very pale brownish-gold colour, similar to that of champagne.","Alternative form of champaine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/champagne"},{"term":"grape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, round, smooth-skinned edible fruit, usually purple, red, or green, that grows in bunches on female vines of most species of genus Vitis and the self-fertile plants of species Vitis vinifera.","Any woody vine of genus Vitis that bears clusters of grapes; a grapevine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing grapes or having a grape flavor.","Of a dark purplish red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zante currant","blocks":[{"text":"Zante currants, Corinth raisins, Corinthian raisins or simply currants, are raisins of the small, sweet, seedless grape cultivar Black Corinth. The name comes from the Anglo-French phrase \"raisins de Corinthe\" and the Ionian island of Zakynthos (Zante), which was once the major producer and exporter. It is not related to black, red or white currants, which are berries of shrubs in the genus Ribes and not usually prepared in dried form."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg/330px-Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zante_currant","wikidata":"Q1382423"},{"title":"Champagne","blocks":[{"text":"Champagne is a sparkling wine originated and produced in the Champagne wine region of France under the AOC rules of the appellation, which demand specific vineyard practices, sourcing of grapes exclusively from designated places within it, specific grape-pressing methods and secondary fermentation of the wine in the bottle to cause carbonation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Glass_of_champagne.jpg/330px-Glass_of_champagne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champagne","wikidata":"Q134862"},{"title":"Grape","blocks":[{"text":"A grape is a fruit, botanically a berry, of the deciduous woody vines of the flowering plant genus Vitis. Grapes are a non-climacteric type of fruit, generally occurring in clusters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grape","wikidata":"Q10978"},{"title":"Champagne (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color champagne is a name given for various very pale tints of yellowish-orange that are close to beige. The color's name is derived from the typical color of the beverage Champagne."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3e/Quartz-Topaz-gem7-76d.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champagne_(color)","wikidata":"Q5069879"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Zante_currant_drying_in_Tsilivi.jpg/500px-Zante_currant_drying_in_Tsilivi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Zante_currant_drying_in_Tsilivi.jpg/500px-Zante_currant_drying_in_Tsilivi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sun-drying Zante currants on Zakynthos, with the grape v